{"trace_id": "altair_datawatch_2018_t04", "title": "[ORG_1] Engineering Inc. / [ORG_2] Corporation — approval risk note", "body": "The acceptance gate is express: the HSR waiting period, including any extension, must have expired or terminated. This is the defined Regulatory Condition in Annex I; it is not merely a general representation about legal compliance. [altair_datawatch_2018__02_merger_agreement__c0108]

The parties must make the HSR filing promptly and no later than the tenth business day after signing, request early termination under the then-agreed process, and not withdraw except in connection with agreement termination. Other required antitrust filings must also be made promptly. The cooperation provisions include sharing specified substantive agency communications and giving the other side’s outside counsel an opportunity to review and comment on planned written communications. [altair_datawatch_2018__02_merger_agreement__c0070]

The remedy obligation is sharply limited. Section 6.1(d) does not require [ORG_1] to divest or hold separate assets, license IP, alter contractual relationships, change operations, or accept restrictions on ownership and operation. [ORG_2] cannot discuss or commit to the listed remedies without Parent’s prior written consent in its sole discretion. The practical risk allocation therefore combines a clearance condition and procedural cooperation with substantial buyer control over substantive concessions. [altair_datawatch_2018__02_merger_agreement__c0072]", "artifact_directory": "artifacts"}

{"trace_id": "[PERSON_7]", "title": "[PERSON_8] approval risk note", "body": "The two votes use different tests. At the Scheme Meeting, approval requires a majority in number representing at least 75% in value of members or the relevant class present and voting, personally or by proxy. At the general meeting, the shareholder resolution requires at least 75% of the total voting rights of eligible members present and voting. The contractual definition therefore preserves a headcount element for the scheme vote that does not appear in the general-meeting test. [[PERSON_2]]

Article VIII also requires court sanction, absence of a continuing prohibitory order or illegality, expiration or termination of the HSR waiting period, and expiration, termination or receipt of the scheduled other regulatory-law waiting periods or consents. These are actual common closing conditions. [[PERSON_5]]

Sanction and effectiveness are separate steps. On the closing date [ORG_2] must deliver the sanctioning order to the Registrar of Companies in England and Wales; that delivery makes the scheme effective. It must also give [ORG_1] the order and appropriate evidence of effectiveness, making delivery evidence a distinct checklist item. [[PERSON_6]]", "artifact_directory": "artifacts"}

{"trace_id": "microsoft_activision_2022_t04", "title": "[ORG_1] Corporation / [ORG_2], Inc. — approval risk note", "body": "The agreement conditions closing on the HSR and specified competition clearances or waiting-period expirations, other specified regulatory approvals, and absence of the described legal restraints. The clearance conditions must be achieved without a Burdensome Condition; the restraint condition also reaches measures imposing or seeking one. [microsoft_activision_2022__01_agreement__c0103]

Both sides undertake reasonable best efforts on filings, information and timely clearance. [ORG_1] makes the final decision on required or advisable filings and, after good-faith consultation and consideration of [ORG_2]'s views, leads regulatory communications, negotiations, timing, strategy and related litigation. The consultation duty therefore survives [ORG_1]'s control of strategy. [[PERSON_6]_agreement__c0083] [microsoft_activision_2022__01_agreement__c0084]

The remedy covenant includes dispositions or licensing of [ORG_2] assets and business restrictions, plus contesting, defending and appealing challenges. But [ORG_1] need not take action reasonably expected to cause a material adverse impact on [ORG_2] as a whole, a material impact on expected merger benefits, or more than an immaterial impact on any [ORG_1] business or product line. Those are the defined Burdensome Condition limits. The drafting supports a substantial but bounded efforts obligation, not an unlimited concession commitment. [microsoft_activision_2022__01_agreement__c0085]", "artifact_directory": "artifacts"}

{"trace_id": "[PERSON_10]", "title": "[ORG_1] Energy Partners, through Nuclear Engineering Holdings LLC / [ORG_2] Systems, Inc. ([ORG_2] Solutions) — approval risk note", "body": "[ORG_2]’s required approval is adoption by holders of a majority of outstanding shares entitled to vote, in person or by proxy. The agreement identifies this as the only class or series vote needed for the transaction; it is also a condition to all parties’ closing obligations. This is an outstanding-shares threshold, so a simple majority of votes actually cast is not the stated test. [[PERSON_4]] [[PERSON_5]]

The buyer separately benefits from section 6.3(c): governmental consents, clearances, permits, notices and other specified actions must occur, and applicable waiting periods must expire, as set out in the disclosure-letter schedule. The review note should track that contractual category without naming agencies not supplied by the clause. The shared no-impediment condition separately covers specified laws, orders and governmental proceedings that prohibit or materially impede the transaction or payment. [[PERSON_6]] [[PERSON_5]]

On the acquisition vehicle side, [PERSON_11] must adopt the agreement as [PERSON_12] sole member and manager immediately after execution, no later than three business days afterward, and deliver evidence to [ORG_2]. That is an affirmative authorization covenant to track alongside the closing conditions. [[PERSON_7]]", "artifact_directory": "artifacts"}

{"trace_id": "[PERSON_10]", "title": "[ORG_1] Electronics Corporation, through [ORG_1] Electronics Europe GmbH / [ORG_2] Communications S.A. — approval risk note", "body": "The defined Regulatory Approvals expressly include CFIUS, French FDI, UK NSI and Taiwan merger-control approval, plus the necessary or advisable approvals identified in the referenced disclosure schedule. Section 8.2(e) conditions acceptance on approvals or expiration/termination of relevant waiting periods, unless waived by Parent in its sole discretion. The agreement also requires no effective Restricting Law. [[PERSON_4]] [[PERSON_7]]

Shareholder action remains a separate gate: adoption of the [PERSON_8], [PERSON_9] Resolutions and Governance Resolutions at the general meeting or a subsequent meeting is an express offer condition. Receipt of the Confirmatory Japanese Tax Ruling is separately specified. [[PERSON_7]]

The parties must coordinate filings and strategy, cooperate and use reasonable best efforts to obtain clearances promptly; Parent bears filing fees. That efforts covenant has substantial boundaries. Parent, Purchaser and their affiliates are not obligated to divest businesses or assets, alter specified relationships or rights, accept restrictions on retained businesses, or litigate or contest regulatory proceedings and orders. A clearance-risk assessment must preserve those express limitations. [[PERSON_5]] [[PERSON_6]]", "artifact_directory": "artifacts"}

{"trace_id": "renesas_transphorm_2024_t04", "title": "[ORG_1] Electronics Corporation, through [ORG_1] Electronics America Inc. / [ORG_2], Inc. — approval risk note", "body": "The stockholder condition requires the Requisite Stockholder Approval at the stockholder meeting. Section 3.4 defines that approval as a majority of the voting power of outstanding common shares entitled to vote, voting together as one class, subject to its stated assumption regarding the buyer’s section 4.6 representations. It is not a majority merely of votes cast. [[PERSON_7]02_agreement__c0041] [[PERSON_6]]

The HSR condition requires expiration or termination of applicable waiting periods and extensions, or receipt of all requisite consents. The agreement separately requires CFIUS Approval and absence of a prohibitive restraint. An FTC Bureau of Competition form letter substantially in the specified August 2021 form does not itself cause the no-restraint condition to fail. [[PERSON_6]] [[PERSON_3]]

Following the contemplated joint voluntary notice, CFIUS Approval can consist of written clearance with no unresolved national-security concerns, referral followed by presidential nonintervention (including no action within 15 days), or written confirmation that the transaction is not covered. Counsel should therefore collect evidence for the applicable defined route. [renesas_transphorm_2024__02_agreement__c0006]", "artifact_directory": "artifacts"}
